{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Me oh my, I loved him so.
Broken my heart to see him go
Only his return will heal my woe.
Johnny has gone for Soldier
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
I’d sell my rod, I’d sell my reel.
I’d even sell my spinning wheel
To buy my love a sword of steel.
Johnny has gone for Soldier
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
I’ll dye my dress, I’ll dye it red.
I’ll walk the streets and hang my head
Today I found my love is dead.
Johnny has gone for Soldier
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 6}
Oh my baby, oh my love.
No more rainbows, no more doves
I have lost my one true love.
Johnny has gone for Soldier
{end_of_verse}
